<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bochica</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Idacansas, Nemqueteba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bochica was a culture hero and god of the Muisca of the Colombian highlands. In Muisca tradition he came from the east as a bearded old man, taught weaving, farming and moral laws, and opened the Tequendama Falls to drain a flood. He was associated with Sugamuxi, the seat of the high priest of the sun.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bochica.jpg" alt="Bochica" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frank Ballesteros · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bochica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
